# Authoritative Full Suite & Final Closure

Source of truth: `docs/sprints/authoritative-consolidated-full-suite-2-final-closure.md`.
These rules bind every future complete-suite execution and every programme closure.

## Authorisation

1. **One attempt per explicit authorisation.** An authorisation is consumed the
   moment the authoritative run is TRIGGERED, not when it passes. Readiness GO
   is not an authorisation — it only permits ASKING for one.
2. **No automatic rerun.** FAIL, TIMEOUT, CANCELLED, PARTIAL, runner loss,
   wrong SHA, misrouted workflow and platform outage are all terminal. A new
   explicit user authorisation is required. Infrastructure failure is not a
   self-service second attempt.
3. **The canonical path is the only path.** `workflow_dispatch` on
   `foundation-evidence-gates.yml` with BOTH `run_full_suite` and
   `full_suite_policy_override` true while the temporary policy is ACTIVE.
   Never reach a complete suite under another alias, another job name, or by
   running "almost everything".

## Tree identity

4. **The tested tree is immutable from trigger.** No code, test, CI, rule,
   documentation, formatting, evidence, version or dependency change once the
   authoritative attempt starts.
5. **One tree, end to end.** candidate tree == tested tree == merged tree ==
   deployed tree == GO-tag tree. A squash merge may change the SHA; it may
   never change the tree.
6. **No post-PASS evidence commit.** Writing the run id, the counts or the PASS
   into the repository after the run changes the tree and invalidates the very
   evidence it records. Run-specific evidence belongs in the annotated GO tag
   and the CI run.
7. **A post-suite tree change invalidates the suite.** If a durable rule is
   discovered only after PASS, that is a NO-GO and a new authorisation, not a
   quiet amendment.
8. **Base movement is a closure blocker.** If the base advances so that merging
   can no longer reproduce the tested tree, do not merge.

## Retirement of the temporary policy

9. **Never retire the temporary Full-Suite policy inside the closure
   candidate.** With the policy RETIRED, `push` to base is an AUTHORISED
   automatic Full Suite, so merging the candidate would immediately start a
   second, unauthorised run. Retirement is a separate act with its own
   authorisation, performed after closure.

## Measurement honesty

10. **Prefix census is diagnostic; the allocation API is authoritative.** A
    census can only report names it was told about in advance. Temporary
    resource ownership is proven by a private root that is drained to zero.
11. **Unknown-prefix non-canonical allocation fails closed.**
12. **Killing a wrapper does not prove the children died.** Verify child
    processes before declaring isolation.
13. **Shared-evidence suites run serially** unless isolation is proven.
14. **Monitoring and restore-drill WATCH stay truthful.** A WATCH is never
    relabelled GO to reach closure, and restore evidence is never manufactured.
15. **Production diagnostics never use an interactive REPL.** It writes real
    ERROR lines into the application log and pins monitoring to WATCH.
16. **Clinical evidence never returns to public storage.**

## Closure

17. **Full Suite PASS alone is not closure.** Closure additionally requires the
    identical tree merged, deployed on the VPS with exit 0, production health
    and privacy verified, zero new production errors, and the annotated GO tag
    pointing at that same tree.
18. **The deploy runs on the VPS, never locally**, and a started deploy is not
    a successful deploy — only an authoritative exit 0 is.
